Input: {"question": "Where does Peter Reginato work?", "documents": [{"doc_id": "d1", "text": "Title: The Urban Canvas: Peter Reginato's New York City Odyssey\n\nIn the heart of the most populous city in the United States, where steel skyscrapers pierce the sky and the sounds of honking horns and chatter fill the air, a creative genius thrives. Peter Reginato, a renowned American artist, has made New York City his playground, his muse, and his home. For decades, Reginato has been an integral part of the city's vibrant art scene, drawing inspiration from the urban landscape and its eclectic inhabitants. Reginato's journey began in the 1970s, when he first set foot in New York City. The city was a hotbed of artistic expression, with the likes of Andy Warhol, Jean-Michel Basquiat, and Keith Haring pushing the boundaries of contemporary art. Reginato, with his unique blend of abstract expressionism and pop art, quickly found his footing in this fertile ground. His early works, characterized by bold colors and geometric shapes, reflected the city's frenetic energy and its ability to reinvent itself. As Reginato's career took off, he became a fixture in the city's art world. His studio, nestled in the heart of Manhattan, became a hub for creatives, where ideas were exchanged, and collaborations were born. Reginato's art, infused with the city's rhythm and pulse, began to gain international recognition. His paintings, sculptures, and installations were showcased in prominent galleries and museums, solidifying his reputation as a master of contemporary art. One of Reginato's most iconic works, \"Cityscape\" (1985), is a testament to his deep connection with New York City. This large-scale painting, featuring a kaleidoscope of colors and abstract forms, captures the city's essence: its towering skyscrapers, bustling streets, and the endless flow of humanity. The work is a love letter to the city, a celebration of its beauty and complexity. Reginato's involvement in the city'